  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only two experiments are complete. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 0.485 accuracy, while config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) achieves only 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. However, we have no information on whether the RNA representation itself can be improved. Question: config_004 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) changes only the RNA encoder from a linear PCA projection to a learned deep generative representation (scVI), keeping profile setting and all other factors identical to config_001. This cleanly isolates the effect of representation quality. Why this is the best next experiment: With only two data points, the most uncertain and consequential design axis is whether a simple linear projection is sufficient or whether a learned encoder captures biologically meaningful structure that PCA misses. The answer determines whether subsequent experiments should prioritize encoder choice (scgpt, deeper models) or other axes (multiprofile aggregation, multimodal fusion). A single-variable comparison to our current best (config_001) maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

